.TH "EPX\-AVAILABILITY" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-availability \- read and change availability
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability [flags]
epx availability [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads product availability (stock), the tenant\(aqs own availability: on a site with list and get, which require \fB\-\-site\fR, and on every site with search. create, update and delete change the availability of a product on a site, bulk\-create, bulk\-update and bulk\-delete that of many.
.PP
Its reads need no OAuth scope. Its writes require the availability.availability_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx availability bulk\-create"
Create availability in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability bulk\-create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the availability records in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of records, each with the productId and site it is for and the fields that create takes. Emporix advises against a record on a site named main, which aggregates the availability of the other sites.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the availability.availability_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx availability bulk\-delete"
Delete availability in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability bulk\-delete [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the availability records that \fB\-\-file\fR names, a JSON array of objects with the productId and site of each, such as \fB[{"productId": "100200", "site": "AcmeStore_NL"}]\fR. The availability of a bundle is that of its scarcest product and cannot be deleted.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Deletes the availability that \fB\-\-file\fR names with one request, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type the tenant at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the availability.availability_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx availability bulk\-update"
Upsert availability in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability bulk\-update [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the availability records in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of records as bulk\-create takes them, or creates those that do not exist (an upsert).
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the availability.availability_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx availability create"
Create the availability of a product on a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability create PRODUCT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the availability of the product PRODUCT_ID on the site \fB\-\-site\fR names, from \fB\-\-file\fR: a JSON object with stockLevel, available, popularity and distributionChannel (ASSORTMENT, HOME_DELIVERY or PICKUP), as \fBepx availability get PRODUCT_ID \-\-site S \-o json\fR prints them. Emporix answers 409 Conflict when the product has one on that site already. It advises against a record on a site named main, which aggregates the availability of the other sites. PRODUCT_ID is the product id (as in \fBepx products list\fR), not its code.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the availability.availability_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx availability delete"
Delete the availability of a product on a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability delete PRODUCT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the availability of the product PRODUCT_ID on the site \fB\-\-site\fR names. The availability of a bundle is that of its scarcest product and cannot be deleted. PRODUCT_ID is the product id (as in \fBepx products list\fR), not its code.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type PRODUCT_ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the availability.availability_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx availability get"
Show the availability of a product on a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability get PRODUCT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads product availability (stock) on the site \fB\-\-site\fR names, the tenant\(aqs own availability. PRODUCT_ID is the product id (as in \fBepx products list\fR), not its code. The availability of a bundle\(aqs products is only in \fB\-o json\fR (bundleAvailabilities).
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among PRODUCT, SITE, STOCK, AVAILABLE, CHANNEL.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.SS "epx availability list"
List the availability of every product on a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads product availability (stock) on the site \fB\-\-site\fR names, the tenant\(aqs own availability. A bundle is listed as a whole and per product; an unknown site lists nothing.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among PRODUCT, SITE, STOCK, AVAILABLE, CHANNEL.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx availability search"
Search the availability of products.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability search [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the availability records, on every site, that an Emporix q filter finds (\fB\-\-query\fR; without it, every record), shown as list shows them, bundles left out. \fB\-\-body\fR with a JSON array of product ids reads theirs instead, bundles included.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among PRODUCT, SITE, STOCK, AVAILABLE, CHANNEL.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, sent as given in the request body, not in the URL (empty: no filter), e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx availability update"
Upsert the availability of a product on a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx availability update PRODUCT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the availability of the product PRODUCT_ID on the site \fB\-\-site\fR names with the one in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object as create takes it, or creates it where there is none (an upsert). The availability of a bundle is that of its scarcest product and cannot be set. PRODUCT_ID is the product id (as in \fBepx products list\fR), not its code.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the availability.availability_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
